## Introduction
Motif-programming is a method for constructing artificial proteins by embedding peptide motif(s) within artificial protein sequences. Recent advances in genome science have revealed a variety of naturally occurring motifs. In addition, evolutionary molecular engineering has enabled us to create artificial motifs that interact with selected target molecules assigned by the researchers. Motif-programming is
